# Affine equiangular 12-sets in the `X_5` lattice slice

| Profile | Value |
|---|---|
| Track | **B** — an exact generic search exists and is reported |
| Native domain | geometry |
| Object regime | exact rationals |
| Computational core | exact linear algebra |
| Certificate | 12-by-10 signed coordinate matrix |
| Intended intuition | symmetry: recover the conjugated `S_4` orbit |
| Domain essentiality | native; no reduction |

## Problem and trust model

This generator turns Lin–Munemasa–Taniguchi–Yoshino, [*Sets of equiangular
lines in dimension 18 constructed from A9 + A9 + A1*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.06377),
into an exact witness task.  The solver receives signed coordinates for vectors
in the paper's `X_5` slice and must return twelve displayed vectors.  A sign row
`s` represents `(s/2, 0^10, (1/2,-1/2))`; `verify` checks candidate membership,
norm/shape conditions, and every integer dot product.  It accepts any valid
twelve-row witness and never reads the planted answer.

Generation is theorem-backed.  Definition 5.2 gives twelve five-subsets;
Lemma 4.2 turns intersection sizes 2 or 3 into affine inner products 0 or 1,
and Lemma 5.3 proves the set is maximum.  The generator carries that certificate
through a uniform coordinate permutation and independent switching mates, then
adds rows drawn from the same 252-vector `X_5` population.  No instance is
solved during generation.

## Why Track B

This is not a Track-A claim.  Section 5 explicitly constructs the 126 switching
classes and Lemma 5.4 uses Magma to enumerate all **151,200** maximum compatible
sets.  The local reference implementation is exact branch-and-bound with
worst-case `O(m^2 d + 3^(m/3))`; at the shipping preset it solves 8/8, averaging
3,855.5 search nodes, 165,210 counted operations, and 0.084 seconds.

The compact route uses the two displayed conjugates of the `S_4` generators.
The planted set is the unique complete orbit of size twelve.  Enumerating the
eight small orbits takes 252 coordinate-permutation applications and 48 exact
lookups, with no arithmetic inner products.  That 300-step symbolic route is
short enough in context; the generic 165k-operation search is not.  Lemma 5.4
is also the paper result that rules out pretending this is structural Track-A
hardness.

