codex
Implemented the native geometric Track B generator based on the paper’s `X_5` construction and verified it against the [current arXiv v3 text](https://arxiv.org/html/2503.06377v3).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.06377/gen_2503_06377.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.06377/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.06377/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.06377/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.06377/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.06377/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

G1–G8 pass locally. The four non-reference attacks scored 0/8; the disclosed Track B exact search succeeds 8/8 at roughly 161,000 operations per instance. Answers are 444 characters and 120 atoms.

The result is not submission-ready: every bare, hinted, and placebo oracle redraw returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” leaving zero scored attempts. Consequently G9(b) remains false and `all_passed=false`. A replenished `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to rerun the three harness arms.
