codex
The audit found two concrete issues worth fixing before any new oracle spend: the demo was not actually the smallest supported instance, and the final escalation to all 252 oriented rows collapses every seed to the same problem up to relabelling. I’m changing the demo to 12 rows, stopping escalation at a diverse 249-row level, and tightening random guessing so it never samples the trivially impossible pair consisting of a row and its switching mate.
