The transcript audit caught exactly the false-negative the contract warns about: one `medium` reply contained a complete tagged matrix but used `+1`, matching the displayed row notation; strict JSON parsing rejected it. I am fixing both sides of the contract—displaying rows as JSON-valid `1/-1` and accepting harmless unary plus—then I must discard this verdict and rerun the bare loop. The other unparsed reply never reached a closing answer tag, so that one is a genuine incomplete response.
apply patch
